1) Inheritance Mode (Domain/Class/Event Type Propagation)
🎯 Goal

Subevents should NOT require repeated:

domain_id
class_type_id
event_type_id

They inherit from their parent event (calendar_event:336).

🧠 Core Rule Change
Before

Each subevent is fully specified:

subevent = independent semantic unit
After
subevent = structural unit + inherited semantics
🏗️ Inheritance Contract
Source of truth
parent_event (calendar_event:336)
Inherited fields
domain_id
class_type_id
event_type_id
location_id (optional inheritance)
Override rule

Only allowed if explicitly provided:

subevent overrides parent field ONLY if non-null
⚙️ Implementation Points
1. API Layer (create_calendar_subevent.php)

Replace manual assignment with:

$parent = getCalendarEvent($pdo, $parentEventEntityId);

$payload = array_merge([
    'summary' => $eventLabel,
], array_filter([
    'event_type_id' => $eventTypeId ?? $parent['event_type_id'],
    'domain_id'     => $domainId     ?? $parent['domain_id'],
    'class_type_id' => $classTypeId ?? $parent['class_type_id'],
    'location_id'   => $locationId   ?? $parent['location_id'],
]));
2. DB behavior (no schema change required)

This is application-level inheritance only:

no denormalization
no copy-on-write required
3. Ensurer layer (important)

Ensure:

calendar_node_ensurer

does NOT overwrite inherited fields.

📬 New Minimal Sub-event Payload (after change)

You will reduce from this:

{
  "operation": "createCalendarSubevent",
  "parent_event_entity_id": "...",
  "event_label": "...",
  "event_type_id": "...",
  "domain_id": "...",
  "class_type_id": "..."
}
To this:
{
  "operation": "createCalendarSubevent",
  "parent_event_entity_id": "calendar_event:336",
  "event_label": "Correct mechanics demonstrated"
}
🧠 Why this matters structurally

You are enforcing:

time defines context
event defines semantics
subevent defines sequence + nuance

This removes:

duplication drift
inconsistent classification
batch payload bloat